upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cloudflare/skills/main/skills/cloudflare/SKILL.md
verified: 2026-08-16
scope: directory
reason: deliberate local edit to the frontmatter description, not drift
note: Full diff 2026-08-16 — both files 248 lines, single-line difference on
  the `description:` frontmatter field. Upstream ends "...Use for any
  Cloudflare development task. Biases towards retrieval..." Local replaces
  that clause with a sibling-routing sentence: "Use as the default entry
  point for Cloudflare work and for anything spanning several products.
  Prefer the narrower sibling when the task sits squarely inside one of
  them — workers-best-practices for reviewing or authoring Worker code,
  wrangler for CLI and wrangler.jsonc, durable-objects for stateful
  coordination, agents-sdk for stateful agents and Workflows, sandbox-next
  or sandbox-stable for sandboxed code execution, cloudflare-email-service
  for email,
  cloudflare-one for Zero Trust and SASE." This is AUDIT-H-04's fix so
  Claude routes to the narrower sibling skill instead of always loading
  this one. Body content otherwise matches upstream exactly.
would_lose_if_wired: an unguarded byte-for-byte refresh would drop the
  sibling-routing clause and reintroduce the ambiguity AUDIT-H-04 fixed.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh skips this directory when .local-fork is
  present, before any fetch or write.
to_vendor: accepted as a permanent managed fork on 2026-08-17. Keep the local
  routing clause because discovery correctness outranks byte-identical vendoring.
  Re-evaluate only if upstream adopts an equivalent narrow-skill boundary; no
  external publication is required.

updated: 2026-08-16 — the clause named `sandbox-sdk`, which upstream retired.
  It now names `sandbox-next` / `sandbox-stable`. Worth noting for the vendoring
  decision: upstream's own successor skills route between each other in their
  descriptions the same way ("Not for X, use Y"), which is the pattern this
  fork adds by hand. That is evidence the clause would be accepted upstream
  rather than rejected as a local preference.
